  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added fail-closed case-wise affine successful-result summaries and a structural fixed point for monotone scalar countdown loops. Raising preflights now decompose true conjunctions and false disjunctions, starting missing fixed-width operands from their declared domains while accepting condition-local literals only from unique same-list dominating producers. Summary cases retain path comparisons, specialize them at caller arguments, and bind every transitive dependency through graph authority. A separate analysis with no summaries recovers only independently derivable arithmetic, buffer, and validated-view proofs; it has no call-fact channel and cannot authorize direct edges. Summary-tainted direct-parameter views remain validated at runtime without materialized descriptors. The frozen catalog integration proves the six requested short-powu copy edges plus one independently exposed evaluation edge unconditional, preserves all 7,081 outputs and nine malformed cases, keeps zero view descriptors, reduces ELF text by 128 bytes, and improves pooled paired time from 2.341237838 ms to 2.210680477 ms (5.58%, all 14 pairs favorable). Focused authority tests, architecture checks, strict baselib checks, and the complete native suite pass.",
    "risks": [
      "The scalar loop theorem is intentionally narrow: conjunctions must expose a signed comparison against a singleton threshold, the induction variable has exactly one direct positive-constant decrement, and loops with control transfer or competing writes remain checked.",
      "Case specialization currently refines direct parameter comparisons only. More complex affine predicates remain conservative and cannot authorize a direct edge.",
      "The independent pass intentionally sacrifices summary-derived precision. It may attach only claims re-derived from guards, local operations, and ordinary checked calls; direct-edge selection remains exclusively summary-aware.",
      "pnpm test:changed stopped at an initially absent FLINT addon. The subsequent required pnpm test:native preparation built that addon and the complete native correctness and performance suite passed."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Treat int64_shift_right as a separate follow-up: its constant-two floordiv can compose cleanly only after a narrow Python-floor singleton-divisor proof excludes zero and INT64_MIN/-1; do not broaden directResultFailureFree generically.",
      "Keep unsupported scalar loops and non-parameter case predicates on the checked fallback until separately proved and mutation-tested.",
      "Use the same isolated-proof pattern for the remaining convolution, reduction, modular-inverse, length-preflight, and characteristic-two fixed-width islands."
    ]
  }
